Inventory every ordinary backend-to-TUI state transfer and action result carrying replacement state. Start with TuiRuntimeOptions, TuiRuntimeStateSnapshot, TuiSubmitResult and reload results, interactive_tui.cpp setup/state_snapshot construction and consumers in runtime_state.*, runtime_views.*, selectors and rendering. Include session metadata, modes, context counts, catalogs/generations, settings, themes, trust, overview, todos, model/session/user-turn selectors and backend-created presentation objects. Follow producers and call sites as well as names.

Classify each field by effect before assigning a domain. UnlockedData holds only backend-affecting facts that are or may become visible: the active agent receiving next Enter, model/provider/variant and execution reasoning, directories especially workspace root, and used tokens are required coverage. Investigate actual selected-agent authority, all selection writers and tests; UI labels establish no authority. Record owners/writers, initial/subsequent paths, consumers, formatting, unknown/loading/empty/error semantics, copying cost, generations and verification. Pure themes/keybindings/preview, selector controls and render preferences stay in src/ava/tui, app/tui or tui-named files, tui-thread-only without locks/UnlockedData. Draft text remains exclusively frontend-owned until submitted as a string. Separate execution reasoning from reasoning display and attachment authority from image rendering. Distinguish immutable dependencies and error/action/control outcomes from replacement state piggybacked on commands.

Produce a source-backed artifact with a contents entry. Every path identifies its backend migration, frontend-local ownership correction, legitimate action contract or explicit deferred history exception, with applicable removal and regression targets. Preserve existing history/streaming and applicable history-backed inspector/picker content paths: history cannot be copied wholesale into UnlockedData; future backend list/vector access needs separate design, not a new journal or migration here. Enumerate retained paths narrowly so agent, directory, model, run or usage facts cannot hide in the exception. Account for all options, returns and exposed backend types without wrapping the bulk snapshot or renaming views; reconcile overlaps before implementation.
